  "id": "014dc5e6-bca4-5fbd-af03-51a9a6de3d55",
  "slug": "super-deluxe-steak-nachos",
  "name": "Super Deluxe Steak Nachos",
  "recipe_type": "appetizer",
  "brief_description": "These steak nachos from Chef John may become your all-time favorite appetizer! Tortilla chips topped with tender strips of steak, beans, cheese, avocado, and more!",
  "cuisine": "Tex-Mex",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "To cook the steak: Season both sides of steak with salt and peppers. Heat oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. Cook steak, turning occasionally, to medium doneness, about 6 minutes per side. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read 135 to 140 degrees F (60 degrees C). Transfer steak to a bowl and let it rest."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Pour a splash of water into the skillet; stir to scrape up browned bits and deglaze the pan. Pour this liquid over meat. Allow meat to cool completely."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "When meat is completely cool, slice thickly (about 1/2 inch) with the grain, then cut into thinner strips. Dice by cutting into pieces against the grain. Transfer chopped steak back to the bowl; toss with the pan drippings."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "To make the beans: Melt bacon fat over medium heat in a pot. Add onion and a pinch of salt; cook and stir until softened, 5 to 6 minutes. Stir in oregano. Add pinto beans and water. Bring back to a simmer and cook until onions are soft, about 5 more minutes. Reduce heat to low."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Mash beans with a potato masher to your desired consistency. Add additional liquid if necessary to achieve your preferred texture. Add the remaining salt to taste. Remove from heat."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F (230 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "To assemble the nachos: Place tortilla chips about 2 or 3 deep in a heat-proof pan. (You may need more than one pan.) Top chips with spoonfuls of beans and a generous handful of steak pieces. Sprinkle with grated cheese."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until cheese is melted and edges start to brown, about 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Scatter tomato, avocado, onion, and jalape\u00f1o over the top. Drizzle nachos with sour cream and garnish with chopped cilantro."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 16,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 35,
